  "summary": {
    "en": "Violence continues in South Sudan with armed attacks by rebel and SPLA-IO forces killing civilians in Tonj East and Warrap State, including women, children and a football referee shot in the head. Intercommunal clashes in Tonj East have prompted UNMISS to support deterrence efforts, while a separate attack in Greater Pibor left three dead and one wounded. MSF suspended all activities in Yei River County after staff were abducted. A rights group demanded justice for survivors of sexual violence, and the UNDP resident representative issued a message of solidarity. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
